Subtask 3.3: Test Placement Rule Failover
Let's test how placement rules handle cluster failures.

Create a failover-aware placement rule:
cat << EOF > failover-placement-rule.yaml
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: failover-placement
  namespace: placement-demo
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchExpressions:
    - key: environment
      operator: In
      values: ["production"]
  clusterReplicas: 3
  tolerations:
  - key: "cluster.open-cluster-management.io/unreachable"
    operator: "Exists"
    effect: "NoSelect"
    tolerationSeconds: 300
EOF
Apply the failover placement rule:
oc apply -f failover-placement-rule.yaml
Create a monitoring script for failover testing:
cat << 'EOF' > test-failover.sh
#!/bin/bash

echo "=== Failover Testing Script ==="
echo "Monitoring placement decisions every 30 seconds..."
echo "Press Ctrl+C to stop"
echo ""

while true; do
    echo "$(date): Current placement decisions:"
    oc get placementdecision -n placement-demo -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,CLUSTERS:.status.decisions[*].clusterName
    echo ""
    
    echo "Cluster health status:"
    oc get managedclusters -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,AVAILABLE:.status.conditions[?(@.type==\"ManagedClusterConditionAvailable\")].status,JOINED:.status.conditions[?(@.type==\"ManagedClusterJoined\")].status
    echo "----------------------------------------"
    
    sleep 30
done
EOF
Make the failover test script executable:
chmod +x test-failover.sh
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Placement Rule Not Selecting Any Clusters
Symptoms: PlacementRule shows 0 selected clusters

Solution:

# Check cluster labels
oc get managedclusters --show-labels

# Verify placement rule selector
oc describe placementrule <placement-rule-name> -n <namespace>

# Update cluster labels if needed
oc label managedcluster <cluster-name> <key>=<value>
Issue 2: Application Not Deploying to Selected Clusters
Symptoms: Subscription exists but application not deployed

Solution:

# Check subscription status
oc describe subscription <subscription-name> -n <namespace>

# Verify channel exists
oc get channel -n <namespace>

# Check placement decision
oc get placementdecision -n <namespace>
Issue 3: Placement Rule Conflicts
Symptoms: Multiple placement rules selecting same clusters

Solution:

# List all placement rules
oc get placementrule -A

# Check for overlapping selectors
oc get placementrule -o yaml | grep -A 10 clusterSelector

# Adjust selectors to be more specific
